<idea-plugin>
    <id>io.github.rejeb.gcp-dataform-plugin</id>

    <name>Google Cloud Dataform</name>

    <vendor url="https://github.com/rejeb/google-cloud-dataform-plugin">rbenrejeb</vendor>


    <description><![CDATA[
            A comprehensive IntelliJ IDEA plugin that brings full language support for Google Cloud Dataform projects, letting you write, navigate, run and debug SQLX pipelines without leaving the IDE.

            <h2>SQLX Language Support</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Full syntax highlighting for SQLX files, covering embedded SQL, JavaScript and config blocks.</li>
                <li>Smart code completion for built-in Dataform functions (<code>ref()</code>, <code>declare()</code>, <code>publish()</code>, etc.), JavaScript/TypeScript symbols, and Dataform template expressions (<code>${...}</code>), with automatic completion popup on <code>$</code>.</li>
                <li>Native BigQuery SQL dialect support, including syntax validation and real-time error highlighting.</li>
                <li>JSON Schema-powered validation and autocompletion for <code>workflow_settings.yaml</code>, generated dynamically from your project's Dataform configuration.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Config Block Assistance</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Property completion in <code>config { }</code> blocks, scoped to the declared action type and generated from the <code>@dataform/core</code> version installed in the project; inserts a value skeleton matching the property type, or moves the caret to the existing value.</li>
                <li>Value completion for enumerated properties, tags already used in the project, and the action's own columns in <code>columns</code>, <code>clusterBy</code>, <code>uniqueKey</code> and <code>assertions</code>.</li>
                <li><code>partitionBy</code> completion with the BigQuery partitioning expressions matching the column types, plus an inspection and quick fix for <code>partitionBy</code> written as an object.</li>
                <li>Validation of unknown config keys and invalid enumerated values, including legacy shorthand forms (<code>uniqueKey: "id"</code>, dependency targets as objects).</li>
                <li>Quick Documentation (<code>Ctrl+Q</code>) on config keys, describing what each key expects.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Template Expression Evaluation</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><code>${...}</code> expressions and workflow settings references are folded to their evaluated value, computed with the project Node.js interpreter; click the value to show the source again.</li>
                <li>Quick Documentation on an expression shows its evaluated value.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Compilation &amp; Diagnostics</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Background project compilation on save and while editing.</li>
                <li>Dataform compilation errors and BigQuery dry-run errors placed on the exact tokens of the SQLX file, with inline error chips.</li>
                <li>Editor banner listing the errors that cannot be placed in the file.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>SQLX Preview Editor</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Split editor next to each SQLX file with the action's lineage graph, compiled query and resolved table schema.</li>
                <li>Test preview for unit test files.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Navigation &amp; Code Intelligence</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Jump between references, includes and declarations with <code>Ctrl+Click</code> / <code>Ctrl+B</code>.</li>
                <li>Column-level navigation: <code>Ctrl+Click</code> a column in a SQLX query to jump straight to its declaration in the source table.</li>
                <li>Show Column Usages (<code>Ctrl+Alt+Shift+U</code>, also available from the editor context menu): list every downstream place where a given column is read across the project &mdash; the reverse direction of Go to Declaration.</li>
                <li>Quick Documentation (<code>Ctrl+Q</code>) for table references, resolved schemas, column metadata, and the built-in BigQuery function catalog (signatures, descriptions, examples).</li>
                <li>Clickable links to workflow configuration properties.</li>
                <li>Find Usages on the fields of <code>STRUCT</code> columns.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Refactoring</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>In-place column rename (<code>Shift+F6</code>) with its own dedicated engine: it walks the plugin's column lineage graph to propagate the new name across every file where the column flows, including through <code>SELECT *</code> resolution, incremental actions, and unrelated join chains, then refreshes the resolved schema.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Data Lineage</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Built-in lineage graph view (Open Lineage View action) that visualizes upstream/downstream dependencies between Dataform actions.</li>
                <li>Column-level lineage tracing, so you can trace exactly where a given column's data originates across your pipeline, including through renamed/aliased columns.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Run &amp; Execute</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Native run configurations for Dataform workflows, launched straight from IntelliJ's Run/Debug toolbar.</li>
                <li>One-click gutter icons in the SQLX editor to execute the current action's workflow without leaving the file.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Unit Tests</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Create Dataform Test from the Project view or editor context menu of a table or view: generates <code>definitions/tests/test_&lt;action&gt;.sqlx</code> with one input per dependency and the expected output, pre-filled from the resolved schemas.</li>
                <li>Column completion after <code>AS</code> in <code>input</code> blocks and in the expected output, including the fields of <code>STRUCT</code> and arrays of structs.</li>
                <li>Generate SELECT from schema intention (<code>Alt+Enter</code>) filling an input or the expected output with a typed placeholder row.</li>
                <li>Completion and navigation for the tested dataset and the input names of a test.</li>
                <li>Run tests from the gutter or a dedicated run configuration; results appear in the IDE test runner, with an expected/actual diff for failing tests.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Google Cloud Integration</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Dataform Tools tool window: manage repositories, browse and create workspaces, and push or pull files between the local project and a GCP Dataform workspace.</li>
                <li>Compare File with Remote to diff a local file with its version in the workspace.</li>
                <li>BigQuery query execution in the Services view, with paged results in a data grid.</li>
                <li>Google Cloud authentication status and sign-in prompts in the editor.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Formatting</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Built-in formatter aware of injected SQL, JavaScript and config blocks inside SQLX files.</li>
                <li>Optional integration with Sqlfluff for external, configurable SQL formatting.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Project Tooling</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>New Project wizard to scaffold Dataform projects with the correct structure.</li>
                <li>New SQLX File action with ready-made templates for every Dataform action type: Table, View, Incremental table, Assertion, Operations, Declaration, and Test.</li>
                <li>Automatic Dataform CLI detection, installation and setup.</li>
                <li>Suggests moving <code>dataformCoreVersion</code> from <code>workflow_settings.yaml</code> to the <code>@dataform/core</code> dependency of <code>package.json</code>.</li>
                <li>Disabled actions (<code>disabled: true</code>) are greyed out in the Project view.</li>
                <li>Fast project indexing of Dataform core definitions and JavaScript symbols for responsive completion and search.</li>
            </ul>
    ]]></description>

